commit bf35f37e6a94fd810519bb949cde43c573192ab2
Author: Greg Rundlett <greg.rundlett@gmail.com>
Date:   Thu Aug 28 21:57:23 2025 -0400

    Do not ignore errors in memcache installation
    
    The PECL installation of the PHP-memcache extension was brute force.
    Therefore it would error every deploy once it was installed. And so
    'ignore errors' was on.
    
    Instead, now we look to see whether it is installed;
    register a fact memcached_pecl_installed when it is already present.
    And thus skip installation depending on the circumstance.
    
    Partly addresses issue #144

